---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title={`About | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="The Morning Build is a free daily briefing on the AI and tech stories that matter to people who build software. Read it in two minutes."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="digest">
      <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Keeping up with AI and tech is a job in itself. New models, new
          tools, new chips, new rules, every single day. Reading it all takes
          an hour you don't have. Skipping it means falling behind.
        </p>
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} is the fix: one short briefing every morning with the
          handful of stories that actually matter to people who build
          software. Each story tells you what happened, why it matters, and
          what to watch next. The whole thing reads in about two minutes.
        </p>
        <p>
          No hot takes, no hype, no filler. Every story is grounded in
          reporting from established outlets and links straight to the
          source, so when something touches your work you can go deeper in
          one click.
        </p>

        <h2>How to read it</h2>
        <p>
          A new briefing lands here every morning. Read it with your coffee,
          or point your feed reader at <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> or
          <a href="/atom.xml">Atom</a> and the full briefing comes to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/">Read today's briefing &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
